Title: WINTER IS HERE
Credit: Written by
Author: David Benioff & D.B. Weiss

EXT. WINTERFELL - NORTHERN GATE - DAY

TYRION
You look troubled, Jon. Is it the dead army or the living people that frighten you?

JON SNOW
The dead don't lie.

TYRION
The living do. A wise observation. Unfortunately, lies are what keep kingdoms alive.

JON SNOW
Thousands of soldiers are coming, and the great houses are still fighting for a chair.

TYRION
The Iron Throne has made fools of greater men than us.

JON SNOW
I don't want a throne. I want my people to survive.

TYRION
And that's exactly why you might be the king they need.

JON SNOW
I'm not a king.

TYRION
Neither was your brother, Robb, until men started calling him one.

Jon turns towards Tyrion.

JON SNOW
If we lose this battle, there will be no kingdom left to rule.

TYRION
Then we must make our enemies understand something.

JON SNOW
What?

TYRION
That the living must stand together, or the dead will rule everything.

A distant horn sounds. Both men turn towards the northern gate.

JON SNOW
They're here.

TYRION
Then let us hope the gods have a sense of humor.

Jon draws his sword. Tyrion watches as the gates begin to open.

JON SNOW
Winter is here.

